  "derives_from": "INVENTED. There is no Indonesian pronunciation-respelling tradition to borrow, so this table takes its inventory from EYD Edisi V's own letter system (Keputusan Kepala Badan Bahasa No. 0424/I/BS.00.01/2022: huruf vokal a e i o u, the optional diacritic e pepet, gabungan huruf konsonan kh ng ny sy, and the diftong ai au ei oi) and its shape from the one native precedent the survey identifies: KBBI's slash field, which prints ordinary Indonesian spelling between slashes with a full stop between syllables and a diacritic on nothing but e -- mer.de.ka /mekrdeka/, tab.let, ban.teng. That is this feature at miniature scale and it is the only Indonesian convention that is keyed on sound. Deliberately NOT derived from EYD V's Penulisan Unsur Serapan or from PUPI, which are keyed on the source language's spelling; see deviations.",
